Description: Distro Custom: customize a Debian live ISO into your own distribution
 D!sco (Distro Custom) turns a Debian or Devuan live ISO into your own
 distribution, step by step: open the ISO, change what you like, press
 Finish. It uses Debian's own tools only (live-boot, squashfs, xorriso,
 mmdebstrap or debootstrap, chroot, Calamares, optionally live-build);
 nothing of Ubuntu is used (no casper, no PPAs).
 .
 It starts with a Welcome page, then Start (extract an ISO or continue a
 project), then eleven steps with Back, Next and Finish: System, Software,
 Startup, Branding, Look & Feel, Boot, Installer, Files & Terminal, Review &
 Apply and Build. Pictures are set with one click (Set as default, Apply),
 services and programs after login are switched on or off with a tick, and
 the folders of a project can be changed without administrator rights.
 .
 PCs get a hybrid live ISO (BIOS and UEFI); the Raspberry Pi gets an SD-card
 image laid out like Debian's own. ARM64 and RISC-V systems are made through
 qemu-user. Checks before building stop what would break the image, and it
 can be tested in QEMU.
 .
 D!sco was called DistroForge (0.9 Beta) and Eduka-Customizer (up to 0.17
 Alpha); the old commands keep working.
